From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:25:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] Metal diamond engine: extension offsets and counts as
 compile-time constants (snapshot cg30k)

Where the extension data sit in the three buffers, and how many faces, boxes and extensions there are, is the same
for every thread and does not depend on the tiling: these are now constants of the kernel (OFS_*, EXT_*), which is
compiled after the data are packed, so no thread loads them or carries pointers to them across the barriers. 1-4 %
on the GCPW line, the SMA launch and the notch tutorial (paired rounds, loaded machine). diamond_check.sh 72 of 72
identical; emskit fdtd check --lite on six models, debye-check and validate on the Metal engine (15 of 15) pass.

Generated-by: Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
